<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Merca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marka, also spelled Merca, is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benadir">Benadir coast</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, south-west of Mogadishu. A trading town since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it exported grain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> from the Shabelle valley and came under the Ajuran Sultanate, the Geledi Sultanate and the Sultanate of Zanzibar in turn before becoming part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a>.</p></div>
